{"duration_api_ms":137716,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fc4db3a5-1f7b-4d38-b7c9-3b8952fec892","total_cost_usd":1.1389828,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91595,"cache_read_input_tokens":962874,"output_tokens":10676,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3847},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91595,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":96734,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":10676,"cacheReadInputTokens":962874,"cacheCreationInputTokens":91595,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1389828,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3847,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":27,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The judge stage passes for `pay-through-the-provider`: no blocking or major defect. The report is in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/judge.md`.\n\nI ran all four review passes in this session, each with the skill the profile names: ddd, hexagonal, clean-code, and the added dca pass. None of them needed the `dca-knowledge` catalog to settle a question.\n\n**All three criteria are met by what the code does, not just by green tests:**\n- **Authorized payment (browser test):** the customer reaches the review step, and the test checks that the provider stub got exactly one payment request for the total shown on the review page.\n- **Refused payment (integration test):** it goes through the real REST adapter against a WireMock stub answering 402. It checks the customer stays at the payment step and sees the exact refusal message.\n- **Slow provider (integration test):** the same setup, with the stub answering after 5 seconds. The shop's 2-second timeout counts it as unavailable, and the exact unavailable message is checked.\n\n**Three minor findings, recorded but not blocking:**\n- **`failure(..)` is misleading:** it now always means \"refused\". The REST adapter also uses it for confirmation and cancellation, which the provider's contract doesn't have, so it reports a refusal the provider never gave. Nothing reads that result today. The fix is to rename it `refused(..)` and either widen `REFUSED`'s description or give those two cases their own outcome.\n- **Out-of-date exception comment:** `PaymentInitiationFailedException`'s JavaDoc and the matching glossary entry still say the customer sees the provider's reason. The page now shows a fixed message. This is for the document stage.\n- **Out-of-date glossary entry:** `PaymentProviderId` says the sample has a single provider, `mock`. When a provider address is configured, it is `provider` instead. Also for the document stage.\n\nNext is the document stage; I didn't run it.","ttft_ms":3848,"type":"result","duration_ms":138342,"uuid":"88a9b25a-d3dd-408f-9d49-d1bb6b26356c","ttft_stream_ms":2471,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":2471,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
